---
import './versioned.css';
---
<figure class="versioned-figure" data-versioned-fill>
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 1</span>Can the old card come back?</div>
 <div class="controls"><label>Fill rule <select data-rule><option value="plain">Unconditional write</option><option value="revision">Remember revision 2</option><option value="token">Reserve a one-use token</option></select></label><label><input type="checkbox" data-loss /> Lose retained revision knowledge</label></div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="board" aria-hidden="true">
   <div class="station app">App A</div><div class="station source">Source</div><div class="station writer">App B</div><div class="station cache">Cache · P7</div>
   <svg viewBox="0 0 600 280" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="M90 95 L300 95 M300 95 L510 95 L510 215 L90 215 L90 95" /></svg>
   <div class="card" data-card><span>Blue mug</span><strong>GBP 20.00</strong><span>revision 1</span></div>
   <div class="ticket" data-ticket>token A</div><div class="barrier" data-barrier>×</div>
   <div class="knowledge" data-knowledge>revision ≥ 2</div>
  </div>
  <div class="readouts" data-live><div><span>Source</span><strong data-source>GBP 20.00 · revision 1</strong></div><div><span>Cache record</span><strong data-cache>Absent</strong></div><div><span>App A’s publication</span><strong data-result>Not attempted</strong></div></div>
  <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">App A has missed. No source read has happened yet.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="controls"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 7</span><span data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span></div>
 <figcaption>An illustrative schedule. The card moves from the source to App A, then towards the cache. Deletion tears away the token before the old card arrives. “Remember revision 2” includes a deliberately unsafe choice: after losing the remembered number, it treats missing as zero. P7 means <code>product:v1:north:P7:en-GB:GBP</code>.</figcaption>
 <details><summary>Events in order, as text</summary><ol><li>App A misses. With the token rule, it reserves token A before reading.</li><li>App A reads GBP 20.00, revision 1, and pauses with that card.</li><li>App B commits GBP 22.00, revision 2.</li><li>App B invalidates. Plain deletion leaves the cache empty; the revision rule remembers 2; the token rule deletes token A.</li><li>Optionally remove the remembered revision. Missing is now unknown, not revision zero.</li><li>App A’s late fill succeeds unconditionally. A retained revision 2 rejects it, but the unsafe missing-as-zero rule accepts it after loss. The token rule rejects it because token A is absent.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import './fill.mjs';
</script>
